This snapshot is a modified redistribution of the Perseus Digital Library's
Scaife Viewer plus a set of upstream open-source components. The overwhelming
majority of the code, text, and data is NOT authored by Dan Meany and is
NOT covered by the copyright notices below — see the "Upstream components"
section at the end of this file and /licenses/ in the running app for the
authoritative attribution and license of each upstream piece.

Dan Meany's own contributions are covered by TWO grants, split by kind:

  * SOFTWARE  (scripts, Django apps, tests, Dockerfiles, config)
      -> MIT License, section 1 below

  * DOCUMENTATION  (README, CLAUDE.md, SBOM, upgrade analysis — prose)
      -> Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
         section 2 below

The split is deliberate. Creative Commons advises against using CC licenses
for software, and MIT is a poor fit for prose — it grants rights (to "deal
in the Software") that make little sense for a document, and its warranty
disclaimer is written for code. Neither grant changes anything about the
upstream components, which keep their own licenses.

